/**
 * TypeDock central configuration.
 *
 * Copy this file to config.php and edit values for your environment — or let
 * the browser installer generate it for you.
 *
 * Precedence (highest first):
 *   1. Real environment variables (useful for containerized / PaaS deploys).
 *   2. Values returned from this array.
 *
 * This file is executed as PHP, so unlike a plain .env file it never leaks its
 * source even if the webserver momentarily fails to enforce access rules.
 */

